        card("Activity 12: guided conversation with a friend at DLI", "You visit your high school friend, a DLI language student, and ask how studies, military duties and the daily schedule are going. A: ask how his or her studies and training are going; tell your friend he or she will do just fine and ask about the weekday routine; ask the distance from the barracks to school. B: say it’s tough to study while doing physical training at the same time; say you wake up at around 4:30, do physical training and return to the barracks, then take a shower, eat and dress for class; say the school is a bit far, about a mile, and you usually take the bus or just run. A sample:", examples=dlg(_S12)),
        card("Activity 13: role play, a regular student and a DLI student", "You are a student at Monterey Peninsula College and your friend, a DLI student, has a slightly different routine. Use eight to ten present-tense verbs to describe your hourly activities on weekdays. Student A: greet your partner, ask about the regular routine at DLI, say your schedule is different and easier, include three things you do after waking up and before class, two during class and three after class, and ask what time he or she wakes up, the time of the training and three other things. Student B: greet in return, say it is a little difficult to study with physical training every day, tell the time you wake up, the time of the training and three things before, during and after school, say your partner’s schedule is better, and ask about it. A sample:", examples=dlg(_S13)),
        card("Activity 14: challenge yourself", "Choose one and be ready to share it in class: (a) what you normally do during weekends from the time you wake up until you go to sleep; (b) what you normally do during weekdays (open tasks, left out)."),
